**Query Parameters**

| Name | Type | Required | Default | Description |
| ---- | -----| -------- | ------- | ----------- |
| **targetDate** | string | no | current date | target date |

**Response**

If successful, returns a status code of 201 and an empty body. A location item is also returned in the header, giving the UUID of the generated invoice (if any).

Adjust the amount for an invoice item. The system adds a new invoice item of type `ITEM_ADJ` to the invoice. If the invoice was already paid for, the system also adds another invoice item of type `CBA_ADJ` to adjust the credit amount in the next invoice. See [Invoice Examples](https://docs.killbill.io/latest/invoice_examples#_invoice_item_adjustment) for more information.

**Notes:** The `linkedInvoiceItemId` field of the new invoice item points to the id of the invoice item being adjusted.

